# Files consumed/executed inside Linux containers MUST keep LF endings even on
# Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf=true here). A CRLF shell script bind-mounted
# into a container fails with "bad interpreter", and CRLF can trip config
# parsers. Pin LF for the deploy-relevant file types (surgical -- no global
# `* text=auto`, to avoid renormalizing the whole repo).
*.sh         text eol=lf
*.conf       text eol=lf
*.yml        text eol=lf
*.yaml       text eol=lf
Dockerfile   text eol=lf
.env.*       text eol=lf
